<ProductLayout
  productName="SecDoma"
  productSlug="secdoma"
  pageTitle="Support"
  description="Support information for SecDoma Cloud, organisation-managed accounts, and self-hosted deployments."
  canonicalPath="/products/secdoma/support/"
  active="support"
>
  <h2>Get help with SecDoma</h2>
  <p>
    For general support, email <a href="mailto:hello@kitechsoftware.com?subject=SecDoma%20support">hello@kitechsoftware.com</a>. Include the platform, application version, deployment type, and a concise description of the issue.
  </p>

  <h2>Organisation-managed accounts</h2>
  <p>
    When an organisation provides or manages your SecDoma account, contact its administrator first for membership, access, policy, workspace, retention, and account-management issues. The organisation may control those settings rather than KiTech Software.
  </p>

  <h2>Self-hosted deployments</h2>
  <p>
    Contact the operator of the deployment for service availability, backups, local configuration, user administration, data retention, and infrastructure incidents. KiTech Software may not have access to a self-hosted environment.
  </p>

  <h2>Safety and abuse</h2>
  <p>
    Use available in-product reporting and blocking controls. Urgent reports may also be sent to <a href="mailto:hello@kitechsoftware.com?subject=SecDoma%20safety%20report">hello@kitechsoftware.com</a>. Include only the information necessary to investigate the report.
  </p>

  <h2>Security vulnerabilities</h2>
  <p>
    Do not submit suspected vulnerabilities through a general support or public issue channel. Follow the <a href="/legal/responsible-disclosure/">Responsible Disclosure Policy</a> and the contact details on the <a href="/security/">Security page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Useful links</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/products/secdoma/privacy/">SecDoma Privacy Notice</a></li>
    <li><a href="/products/secdoma/delete-account/">Delete a SecDoma account</a></li>
    <li><a href="/privacy/choices/">Exercise privacy rights</a></li>
  </ul>
</ProductLayout>
